      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:1:35:5",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) الْأَيْدِي ثَلَاثَةٌ سَائِلَةٌ وَ مُنْفِقَةٌ وَ مُمْسِكَةٌ وَ خَيْرُ الْأَيْدِي الْمُنْفِقَةُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Jahm Bin Al hakam Al Madainy, from Ismail Bin Abu Ziyad, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘The hands are three – an asking (hand), and a spending (hand), and a withholding (hand); and the best of the hands is the spending (hand)’."
        ]
      }
    },
